"""Update the single project overview with the current tank constraint."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
STUDY=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];ROOT=STUDY.parent;FILE=ROOT.parent/'project-overview.html'
def update():
    c=json.loads((STUDY/'results/calculations.json').read_text());r=json.loads((STUDY/'results/validation.json').read_text());data=json.loads((STUDY/'results/data.js').read_text().split('=',1)[1].rstrip(';'));d=next(x for x in data['cases'] if x['case']==data['default_case']);v=d['final']['regions']['range20to50']['6'];sections=d['final']['sections'];n=c['nominal']
    block=f'''<!-- scuba-source-start -->
<section id="scuba-source"><div class="eyebrow">Current source constraint · 23 Oct 2026</div><h2>Scuba tank → loaded air motor → single outdoor nozzle</h2><p>Current logistics use a scuba cylinder. Reference: 12 L / 200 bar gauge / 30°C, with an assumed 20 bar cutoff. Direct high-pressure connection to the motor is incompatible. Use a supplier-qualified pressure-reduction package; the motor needs 6.3 bar gauge while running and has a 7 bar gauge working-pressure maximum.</p><p><a href="Airflow-Assessment/scuba-study/results/index.html"><strong>Open tank calculations and single-nozzle CFD →</strong></a> · <a href="Airflow-Assessment/scuba-study/results/calculations.json">Real-air inventory / motor equations</a> · <a href="Airflow-Assessment/scuba-study/README.md">Assumptions and limits</a></p><p>One loaded LZB46: 19.4 g/s; 972 L/min free air; external shaft load 840 W / 1270 rpm. Inventory-only runtime: {n['adiabatic_one_motor_s']:.0f}–{n['isothermal_one_motor_s']:.0f} s, or 10–12 complete 10 s pulses. Four motors: 77.6 g/s for about 26–31 s. No extra cold-output receiver selected. Regulator flow, droop, icing, exhaust restriction and the loaded cooling point remain unqualified.</p><p>Executed {r['cases']} new native CFD runs, {r['native_frames']} saved frames. One 280 × 40 mm slot; still air, gravity, 10 s spray. Default {d['case']}: source {d['inputs']['source_c']:.2f}°C from conditional single-motor first law plus assumed heat pickup. At 10 s: {v['volume_m3']*1000:.2f} L / {v['mass_kg']*1000:.2f} g ≥6°C below ambient in the 20–50 cm analysis band. Best sampled 5 × 5 cm drop: {sections[0]['best_sampled_5cm_mean_drop_k']:.2f} K at 20 cm; {sections[2]['best_sampled_5cm_mean_drop_k']:.2f} K at 50 cm.</p><p class="sub">These are numerical air-field predictions with assumed source boundaries. Not a person/comfort result. No post-shutoff decay or tank-to-CFD transient coupling. Two-grid sensitivity is not an accuracy bound. Ten balance/EOS checks pass; no new Lean or hardware validation. Earlier compressor and four-motor CFD remain separate historical options. Next: confirm cylinder stamp, tank-valve connection, rated full-flow regulator package and sustained motor load; measure the source before fabrication.</p></section>
<!-- scuba-source-end -->'''
    block=block.replace('</section>', '<p><a href="Airflow-Assessment/scuba-study/results/index.html#shaft-load-22"><strong>Shaft-load sketch and 22°C sensitivity →</strong></a>. The 19.4 g/s point is already loaded (840 W at 1270 rpm); free speed is 2400 rpm. If motor inlet is 22°C, the conditional first law gives −21.04°C motor exhaust and −0.46°C at the nozzle with inherited path UA / 30°C ambient. A 22°C tank does not fix motor inlet temperature. Unloaded airflow/temperature remain unknown. Eight algebra/EOS checks pass; no new CFD, Lean or hardware validation.</p></section>')
    block=block.replace('</section>', '<p><a href="Airflow-Assessment/scuba-study/results/index.html#motor-options"><strong>POC motor alternatives / procurement →</strong></a> · checked 24 Oct 2026. Three Gast models plus two operating points for 2AM compared with LZB46 using paired manufacturer curves. First bench candidate: 2AM-NCC-16 at about 200 W / 8.4 g/s / 5.6 bar / 1000 rpm. Conditional motor drop about 24 K; short-path UA=1 W/K is assumed. Standard Gast exhaust requires lubrication and containment, not person-facing release. Local supply routes verified: Goodwin Dubai offers Gast; Mechatronics Dubai lists GLOBE V1/V2/V4; TAHAS Istanbul is in the Gast distributor locator. UAE/Turkey are not ruled out. Exact local stock and dispatch remain unconfirmed. GLOBE needs paired curves before thermal ranking. US Zoro listings also verified; no destination delivery date confirmed. Thirty arithmetic checks pass. No new CFD/Lean/hardware validation. Motor-only cooling must be separated from regulator-only cooling with measured flow, temperatures and shaft power. Steady cooling budgets added: 20 energy/mixing checks; Gast candidates have conditional bench cooling potential. Outdoor >6 K at 20–50 cm remains unverified. GLOBE V1 lacks paired airflow, so its 520 W listing cannot yet establish a temperature drop. <a href="Airflow-Assessment/scuba-study/results/index.html#motor-shopping">28 Oct motor shopping specification</a>: paired 20–30 K motor-drop screen at 10–20 g/s; assumed 25% heat return gives 268–805 W depending on flow/drop. Standalone pneumatic motors only. Air-drill listings removed from the shortlist after the scope correction. No suitable standalone motor under $100 or qualified Turkish motor checkout listing verified. Gast 1AM/2AM/4AM remain standalone alternatives; stock and delivery unconfirmed. <a href="Airflow-Assessment/scuba-study/evidence/motor-options/SF-week-check-2026-10-28.json">28 Oct SF one-week delivery check</a>: lowest previously observed standalone candidates are Gast 1AM ($256.99) and 2AM ($313.99), before tax/shipping. No arrival by 4 Nov verified; supplier checks blocked or inconclusive. No sub-$100 qualified option found. This does not establish absence of local stock.</p></section>')
    text=FILE.read_text();start='<!-- scuba-source-start -->';end='<!-- scuba-source-end -->'
    if start in text:a,b=text.split(start,1);_,z=b.split(end,1);text=a+block+z
    else:text=text.replace('<!-- mass-flow-sweep-start -->',block+'\n<!-- mass-flow-sweep-start -->',1)
    if 'href="#scuba-source"' not in text:text=text.replace('<nav aria-label="Sections">','<nav aria-label="Sections"><a href="#scuba-source">Scuba source</a>',1)
    FILE.write_text(text)
if __name__=='__main__':update()
